4	f	1	My part-time job yesterday was hilarious! I barely made it on time and dashed into the staff room. I was like, I made it! I’m ready to work! But as it wasn’t a busy day, the teachers there were gossiping about their love lives, just passing the time. What’s more, it wasn’t a lighthearted story—one of the teachers had just broken up with her boyfriend after eleven years together. I kept thinking, ‘Is it okay for me to be here…?’ the whole time\n(「funny part time job」だと「面白いアルバイト」という意味が曖昧になるため、「My part-time job yesterday was hilarious!」と自然な表現に変更しました。元の日本語の感情をより反映しています。)\nI went to a funny part time job yesterday \n↓\n My part-time job yesterday was hilarious!	4	2025-08-23 04:32:43.752029	2025-08-23 04:32:43.752029
5	f	2	My part-time job yesterday was hilarious! I barely made it on time and dashed into the staff room. I was like, I made it! I’m ready to work! But as it wasn’t a busy day, the teachers there were gossiping about their love lives, just passing the time. What’s more, it wasn’t a lighthearted story—one of the teachers had just broken up with her boyfriend after eleven years together. I kept thinking, ‘Is it okay for me to be here…?’ the whole time\n(「run into」は「偶然出会う」という意味合いが強いため、「dashed into」に変更して「急いで入る」というニュアンスを明確にしました。また、「waiting room for doctors」は文脈から「控え室」と訳されるため、「staff room」と自然な表現にしました。)\nI made it in time and run into the waiting room for doctors \n↓\n I barely made it on time and dashed into the staff room	4	2025-08-23 04:32:43.771676	2025-08-23 04:32:43.771676
