8	306	314	620	{\n  "answer_1": {\n    "content": "Yes, 取り組みました generally means 'worked on' or 'tackled' something, often implying a sense of effort or initiative.",\n    "explanation_en": "The verb 取り組む (とり.くむ) means to engage in or tackle a task or challenge with determination. When used in the past tense as 取り組みました, it conveys that you actively worked on something, often with a sense of purpose or effort. It is frequently used in personal or reflective contexts like journals to emphasize the process or dedication rather than just the completion of a task."\n  },\n  "answer_2": {\n    "content": "Example sentence: 新しいプロジェクトの計画に取り組みました。",\n    "explanation_en": "This translates to 'I worked on the planning of a new project.' Here, 取り組みました highlights the effort and engagement in the planning process, making it sound proactive and dynamic, much like in your journal entry about working on the load test environment setup."\n  },\n  "answer_3": {\n    "content": "Additional note on nuance",\n    "explanation_en": "While 取り組みました can often be replaced with simpler expressions like しました, it adds a layer of personal involvement or challenge to the action. It’s particularly suitable for journals or contexts where you want to reflect on your efforts or approach to a task, as seen in your revised sentence '構築に取り組みました' which sounds more engaging than '構築作業をしました.'"\n  }\n}	3	9	8	2025-08-26 10:40:55.662369	2025-08-26 10:40:55.662369
