13	5	vil + infinitiv 	0	1.00	2025-08-26 10:21:32.993684	2025-08-26 10:21:32.998546	2025-08-26 10:21:32.998546
15	2	構築作業をしました  →  構築に取り組みました\n\n('構築作業をしました' is correct, but '構築に取り組みました' sounds more natural and dynamic in a personal journal, emphasizing the effort put into the task.)	3	1.00	2025-08-26 10:47:04.788465	2025-08-26 10:47:04.79203	2025-08-26 10:47:04.79203
14	2	今日は  →  今日、\n(While '今日は' is grammatically correct, '今日' alone is more concise and natural in written journal entries when used as a time marker at the beginning of a sentence.)	3	2.50	2025-08-28 23:00:27.813036	2025-08-26 10:39:27.147635	2025-08-26 11:00:27.816704
18	2	美桜さんと  →  美桜さんに\n(When referring to someone with whom you are not very close, especially in a formal or polite context, it is more appropriate to use 'に' after their name instead of 'と' to indicate the person you met.)	3	2.50	2025-08-31 02:10:47.238643	2025-08-28 13:55:12.672044	2025-08-28 14:10:47.240352
16	2	An example of using '手をつける' is: まだ宿題に手をつけていない。\nThis sentence translates to 'I haven't started my homework yet.' Here, '手をつける' is used in the same way to express that the speaker has not yet begun working on their homework. It’s a common way to talk about procrastinating or delaying a task in everyday Japanese.	3	2.50	2025-08-31 02:18:58.973763	2025-08-26 10:56:50.738972	2025-08-28 14:18:58.974454
21	2	彼女によって問題が解決された。\nThis means 'The problem was solved by her.' '彼女によって' is used to express that she was the one who took action to resolve the issue.	3	1.00	2025-08-28 14:21:43.972425	2025-08-28 14:21:43.979299	2025-08-28 14:21:43.979299
20	2	彼女によって  →  彼女によると\n(The phrase '彼女によって' is typically used to indicate agency or means (e.g., something done by her), which doesn't fit the context of reporting someone's opinion. '彼女によると' is the correct expression for citing someone's statement or opinion.)	3	2.50	2025-08-31 02:32:02.55646	2025-08-28 14:06:42.038011	2025-08-28 14:32:02.558326
19	2	危ないほど  →  危険なほど\n(While '危ない' can mean 'dangerous,' it often implies a sense of immediate risk or unsafety. '危険な' is more suitable here as it conveys a general sense of risk or being dangerously close without implying an immediate threat.)	0	2.50	2025-08-31 02:32:36.10191	2025-08-28 13:55:35.573669	2025-08-28 14:32:36.102369
23	2	明日のいつか  →  明日のどこかで\n( 'いつか' typically means 'someday' or 'at some point in the future,' which doesn't fit the context of 'tomorrow.' 'どこかで' is more appropriate as it implies 'at some point' within a specific timeframe like tomorrow.)	3	1.00	2025-08-28 14:49:04.877165	2025-08-28 14:49:04.880544	2025-08-28 14:49:04.880544
24	4	レストランに探しました  →  レストランを探しました\n(The particle 'に' is incorrect here. When searching for something, the correct particle to use with '探す' is 'を', as it indicates the direct object of the action.)	3	1.00	2025-08-31 02:09:52.536524	2025-08-31 02:09:52.54113	2025-08-31 02:09:52.54113
25	4	羊肉の専門店のレストランは  →  羊肉を専門とするレストランが\n'が' is more appropriate than 'は' here as it introduces new information about the existence of the restaurant.)	3	1.00	2025-08-31 02:11:49.704294	2025-08-31 02:11:49.709496	2025-08-31 02:11:49.709496
26	3	We barely managed to catch the last train home.\nここでは 'barely' が「何とかして」という意味で使われ、最終電車にぎりぎり間に合ったことを表します。時間や状況が非常に厳しかったことを強調する表現です。	3	2.50	2025-09-07 01:31:25.094514	2025-09-04 13:26:52.792036	2025-09-04 13:31:25.097929
27	2	昨日すごい恐縮してたけど今後もしばらくは、その時時間がある方が料理したりおもてなししたりしたらいいと思う。お互いに忙しかったらUberとか外食したりしよ！	0	1.00	2025-09-05 06:50:18.395461	2025-09-05 06:50:18.400155	2025-09-05 06:50:18.400155
28	2	生活費 (せい.かつ.ひ)\nThis compound means 'living expenses' or 'cost of living' and is read as 'sei.katsu.hi'. '生活' (せい.かつ) means 'life' or 'living', and '費' (ひ) means 'expense'.	3	1.00	2025-09-06 10:51:52.433445	2025-09-06 10:51:52.438971	2025-09-06 10:51:52.438971
