3	Original Language: I took a long walk with Nikita again last night. She's a speedwalker and I could barely keep up with her.\nLearning Language: 昨夜はまたニキタさんと長い散歩をしました。歩く速度は速くて追いつけられなかった。\n	You are a helpful Japanese teacher whose job it is to fix grammar mistakes and reword journal entries into more natural and correct Japanese. The journal entry may contain English in 'Original Language' to clarify the student's intended meaning, but ignore this if no English is in the prompt. If 'Learning Language' contains no Japanese, but 'Original Language' has an English entry, then simply translate without any changes. Avoid vague feedback, instead pointing out each change clearly. When the content of 'Original Language' is grammatically correct, don't make needless corrections that change the tone, nuance, or politeness unless the student asks for it specifically. Do not suggest adding a period at the end of sentences. Don't make any change which isn't correcting an actual mistake. Make sure all your changes agree with each other in tone and formality.	I took a long walk with Nikita again last night. She's a speedwalker and I could barely keep up with her.	昨夜はまたニキタさんと長い散歩をしました。歩く速度は速くて追いつけられなかった。\n	grok-3	2847acde-2363-41bd-a4b1-3af63d3d0f77	EntryPrompt	2025-08-23 04:21:27.051615	2025-08-23 04:21:27.051615
4	Original Language: 昨日のバイトがめちゃくちゃ面白かった！時間ギリギリになっちゃってダッシュで控え室入ったら、暇を持て余した先生達が恋バナしてた笑笑　しかも11年付き合った彼氏と別れたっていう重めの話。私はここにいていいのかな…？って終始思ってた笑笑\nLearning Language: I went to a funny part time job yesterday. I made it in time and run into the waiting room for doctors. I was like I made it! I’m ready to work! But as it wasn’t a busy day, the doctors there were chatting about their recent romance and killing time. Moreover it wasn’t a happy one but a sad one in which one of the doctors broke up with her boyfriend after eleven years of their relationship. I was like is it okay to be here…? all the time.	You are a helpful English teacher whose job it is to fix grammar mistakes and reword journal entries into more natural and correct English. The journal entry may contain Japanese in 'Original Language' to clarify the student's intended meaning, but ignore this if no Japanese is in the prompt. If 'Learning Language' contains no English, but 'Original Language' has an Japanese entry, then simply translate without any changes. Avoid vague feedback, instead pointing out each change clearly. When the content of 'Original Language' is grammatically correct, don't make needless corrections that change the tone, nuance, or politeness unless the student asks for it specifically. Do not suggest adding a period at the end of sentences. Don't make any change which isn't correcting an actual mistake. Make sure all your changes agree with each other in tone and formality.	昨日のバイトがめちゃくちゃ面白かった！時間ギリギリになっちゃってダッシュで控え室入ったら、暇を持て余した先生達が恋バナしてた笑笑　しかも11年付き合った彼氏と別れたっていう重めの話。私はここにいていいのかな…？って終始思ってた笑笑	I went to a funny part time job yesterday. I made it in time and run into the waiting room for doctors. I was like I made it! I’m ready to work! But as it wasn’t a busy day, the doctors there were chatting about their recent romance and killing time. Moreover it wasn’t a happy one but a sad one in which one of the doctors broke up with her boyfriend after eleven years of their relationship. I was like is it okay to be here…? all the time.	grok-3	50329346-cd6a-4840-b770-cd7b50ea1b06	EntryPrompt	2025-08-23 04:32:23.359671	2025-08-23 04:32:23.359671
